upx_packed_pe_x86_64.dll -- the win64/pe DLL fixture for `kuna_analysis::upx::pe`.

What it is
  A small MinGW-w64 (llvm-mingw) DLL packed by UPX 5.2.1 with default settings.
  5,632 bytes packed; 7,680 bytes unpacked. PackHeader at 0x1fd: version=13,
  format=36 (win64/pe), method=2 (NRV2B_LE32), filter=0x49.

  A DLL is what makes UPX keep every relocation (20 DIR64 entries here) and move
  the export directory out of the compressed image, so both have to be rebuilt.
  Its exports, from lib.def, cover each kind: a named export (lib_add @1), a
  NONAME ordinal (lib_ord_only @2), another named one (lib_unused @3), and a
  forwarder (lib_fwd = KERNEL32.GetTickCount @4).

  `kuna unpack` writes what `upx -d` (5.3.0) writes except the IAT data directory
  and each import descriptor's OriginalFirstThunk; the export table, relocations
  and imports (as a set) equal the linker's original.

Where it came from
  Built in the mstorsjo/llvm-mingw docker image (clang 23.1.4):

      x86_64-w64-mingw32-clang -O1 -s -shared -o lib.dll lib.c lib.def -Wl,--out-implib,liblib.a
      upx -o upx_packed_pe_x86_64.dll lib.dll                # UPX 5.2.1

  lib.c: three exported int functions reading through a table of int pointers
  (so the image needs relocations), and an empty DllMain.

  sha256(original lib.dll)  74b90be829bd169ea4f0517a580dc15655365cf74ca5d417e5676808eac4b121
  sha256(packed)            759cbdef04671a65d8bce121f4016ca81fb861c95d8b60f1645a45d32eca0eea

Why it is vendored rather than built
  `upx` is not installed on CI, and neither is a MinGW toolchain.
